&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 120%;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 120%;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;Included in the Operating Agreement, WPS and WPL each have the right and option to require the other owner to purchase its share of our capital stock. If both parties decided to put their share of capital stock to the other owner, WPS would buy WPL&amp;#8217;s share of capital stock. The put option purchase price is based upon the exercising party&amp;#8217;s ownership percentage of net worth in us, as explained within the Operating Agreement. Twelve month&amp;#8217;s written notice is required to exercise the put option. As of December&amp;#160;31, 2025, neither owner had provided the required notice to exercise its put option.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 120%;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 120%; font-family: 'Calibri',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
